lesson: 73
title: Some go away: how many are left
stars: 0
explain: A story can start with some things and then some of them go away: given away, lost or sold.
explain: To find how many are left, take the ones that went away from the ones we had.
explain: Ben has 15 cards and gives 6 to Mia: 15 - 6 = 9, so Ben has 9 cards left.
vars: a=name b=name t=thing n=10..90 m=2..40
need: n - m >= 2
answer: n - m
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} gives {m} {t} to {b}. How many {t} does {a} have left?
exercise: There are {n} {t} in a box. {a} takes {m} {t} out. How many {t} are left in the box?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}. {a.He} lost {m} of them. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: A shop had {n} {t}. It sold {m} {t}. How many {t} does the shop have left?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t} and gave away {m}. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: There were {n} {t} on the table. {a} took {m} away. How many {t} are still on the table?
test: Of the {n} {t} that {a} owned, {m} went to {b}. How many does {a} still own?
test: {m} {t} fell out of a bag that held {n}. How many {t} stayed in the bag?
test: {a} started with {n} {t}, but {a.he} has since sold {m}. What does {a.he} have left?
test: How many {t} remain if {a} hands {m} of {a.his} {n} {t} to {b}?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t} and gave {m} of them away. How many {t} are left?
exercise: How many {t} does {a} have left if {a.he} had {n} and gave {m} to {b}?
exercise: {a} has {n} {t}. {a.He} donates {m} to a school fair in Texas. How many {t} does {a.he} still have?
exercise: A bakery in Leeds baked {n} rolls and sold {m}. How many rolls remain?
exercise: {n} birds sat on a fence in Ontario. {m} flew away. How many birds are still on the fence?
exercise: {a} had {n.words} {t}. {a.He} handed out {m.words} to friends. How many {t} does {a.he} have now?
exercise: There were {n} children on a beach in Queensland. {m} went home. How many children are still on the beach?
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}, then lost {m} at the park. How many {t} remain?
test: A Dublin shop sold {m} of its {n} {t}. How many {t} are unsold?
test: {b} received {m} {t} from {a}, who had {n} before. How many does {a} keep?
test: From a crate of {n} {t}, {m} were taken. What number is still in the crate?
test: {n} sheep were in a field in Wales; {m} were moved to another field. How many sheep stayed?
test: {a} passed out {m} {t} from {a.his} {n}. How many {t} remained with {a.him}?
test: Take {m} from {n}: how many are left?
exercise: {a}'s got {n} {t}, gives {m} to {b}. how many left
exercise: {n} {t} in the box, {a} takes {m} out. how many left in it
exercise: {a} had {n} {t}, lost {m+1} — no wait, {m}. how many {a.he} got now
exercise: shop had {n} {t}, sold {m}. Kai says {n+m} left. nah, how many left really
test: {n} {t}, {m} gone, how many still there
test: {a} had {n} {t}, {b} borrowed {m}, and {b}'s got 3 cats lol. how many {a} got left
test: {a} drops {m} of {a.his} {n} {t} down the drain. how many {a.he} got left
exam: Whereas {a} is in possession of {n} {t} and subsequently transfers {m} {t} to {b}, determine the quantity of {t} remaining in the possession of {a}.
exam: It is given that {m} {t} are withdrawn from a receptacle which formerly contained {n}. Ascertain the number of {t} remaining therein.
exam: Compute the remainder when {m.words} is subtracted from {n.words}.
exam: State the residual holding of {a}, whose original stock of {n} {t} has been diminished by {m}.
exercise: {a}'s farm had {n} sheep. In the hard winter, {m} of them didn't make it. How many sheep are left?
exercise: Mum had {n} dollars saved. After she was laid off, she had to spend {m} of it on rent. How many dollars are left?
test: crap, {m} of the {n} {t} in the box are gone — {b} has 'sticky fingers', we all know it. how many still in there
